                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bed and breakfast",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e13d3e7-e05a-3dd9-bae2-16f08ad53a4c",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5f8454-6fd5-34e6-a43b-a3cc6810e03f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A score of 26, made up of a score of 20, 1 and 5 in any order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8943cd6d-ba07-48b1-a954-367548beeb3d",
                                                "sense_id": "5e13d3e7-e05a-3dd9-bae2-16f08ad53a4c",
                                                "text": "The language of darts is a combination of hybrid Cockney slang, metaphor and phrases that “stuck” for no apparent reason except they sounded good. […] Bed ’n’ breakfast—the number 26 when scored by hitting a 20, 5, and 1; comes from the price of a bed and breakfast in Olde England which was 2/6d, two shillings and sixpence."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20955670-42b7-48da-9cd8-9181fc097026",
                                                "sense_id": "5e13d3e7-e05a-3dd9-bae2-16f08ad53a4c",
                                                "text": "This can be a lengthy procedure when neither team can do better than ‘bed and breakfast’ (26)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "424aca7a-2c7e-38f8-928f-1b8cfef843a1",
                                        "entry_id": "ae5f8454-6fd5-34e6-a43b-a3cc6810e03f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The number 26."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e58aa9c4-4a6e-4b4c-9527-adba8110452d",
                                                "sense_id": "424aca7a-2c7e-38f8-928f-1b8cfef843a1",
                                                "text": "Bingo calls that might leave the budding old-timer generally baffled include:[…] 26 ― Bed and breakfast. Traditionally it would cost two and six – two shillings and six pence. Now its £180 a night but you get biscuits."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
